From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0381-oom-fix-02-refused-image-left-out.patch

Source: 0381-oom-fix-02-refused-image-left-out.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches after 0211. Paths are the submodule's.

Mario Kart World on next16 ended in JoinImages: vk::Exception through SlotVector<Image>::insert to
terminate. The image was a sparse tiled one like the 8 before it. MakeImage asks for the sparse image
first, and that was refused (EDEN_SPARSE_IMAGE, stderr line 204, before any mapping line), so it went
on to MemoryAllocator::CreateImage. There `huge` is texels > 2^28 and 16384x16384 is exactly 2^28, so
the real paths were tried, and refused: the kernel would not map it. CreateImage's last step, the
unbacked sparse image, is the same request that had failed, so it failed too. "Format 9" in the log
is VkFormat R8_UNORM and the earlier "format 12" is PixelFormat R8_UNORM: the same format.

So an unbacked image cannot catch this one. It takes 172 mappings, which is what the kernel refused.
A smaller stand-in image would need guest-sized views and attachments it cannot hold. What every
caller of FindImage already handles is no image at all, the answer for an unmapped address:

- A texture gets the null view and reads zero. VisitImageView keeps no view for the descriptor, and
  TickFrame invalidates the tables when the pause ends, so the image is asked for again.
- A render target is left out, as for address 0. FindRenderTargetView returned the null view here,
  a path that could not be reached before: UpdateRenderTargets would prepare its missing image.
- GetBlitImages gives nothing and the blit goes through guest memory.

For an image that is written: nothing lies about holding the data. GPU writes while it is left out
are lost. Guest memory keeps what the guest wrote, and the image is made and loaded from it at the
next use once memory allows, as any new image. For 1 s nothing of the refused size or larger is asked
for, because a refusal took 195 ms here with its reports.

Only this insert is covered: the feedback shadow's insert and exceptions later in JoinImages still
end the session. SlotVector::insert is noexcept on desktop builds, where this still terminates; the
console's copy throws (headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake).

EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS=1 ends the session as before, and so does EDEN_NX2_UNBACKED_LIMIT other
than 0, which is how a session asks to end on refused images.

Proven: PS5-target syntax check with the SDK's libc++, -Wall -Wextra -Werror, real generated sources:
vk_texture_cache_cost.cpp clean, vk_texture_cache_base.cpp (the Vulkan instantiation) only the three
diagnostics already on other lines (248, 1344, 1345), and a static_assert that the requires branches
are taken. prepare-vulkan-port.py skips the same 4 anchors with and without. The OpenGL instantiation
could not be checked (no glad in the harness). Not linked, not run. A guess: how a game looks with
such a texture missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index b2759ab2fd..f4c6dfaeed 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -1365,6 +1365,18 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::Finish() {
     scheduler.Finish();
 }
 
+// EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS=1: an image with no memory ends the session, as it did. So does
+// EDEN_NX2_UNBACKED_LIMIT other than 0, which is how a session is asked to end on those.
+bool TextureCacheRuntime::ImageRefusalEnds() {
+    static const bool ends = [] {
+        const char* const asked = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS");
+        const char* const limit = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UNBACKED_LIMIT");
+        return (asked != nullptr && asked[0] == '1') ||
+               (limit != nullptr && std::strtoul(limit, nullptr, 10) != 0);
+    }();
+    return ends;
+}
+
 StagingBufferRef TextureCacheRuntime::UploadStagingBuffer(size_t size, bool deferred) {
     return staging_buffer_pool.Request(size, MemoryUsage::Upload, deferred);
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
index cc87a5c03e..a3c54dc251 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
@@ -67,6 +67,22 @@ public:
 
     std::optional<StagingBufferRef> TryUploadStagingBuffer(size_t size, bool deferred = false);
 
+    /// Runs `make`, which makes an image, and says if it did: false when the device refused it
+    /// memory and an image with nothing bound too. On the console the exception reaches here
+    /// through the image's slot (headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake).
+    template <typename Make>
+    [[nodiscard]] bool SurvivesImageRefusal(Make&& make) {
+        try {
+            make();
+            return true;
+        } catch (const vk::Exception& refused) {
+            if (refused.GetResult() != VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY || ImageRefusalEnds()) {
+                throw;
+            }
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
     /// The most UploadStagingBuffer always finds room for.
     [[nodiscard]] size_t UploadSliceBytes() const noexcept;
 
@@ -258,6 +274,9 @@ public:
     std::optional<ASTCDecoderPass> astc_decoder_pass;
     std::optional<BcEncoderPass> bc_encoder_pass;
 
+    /// Whether a refused image ends the session (SurvivesImageRefusal).
+    [[nodiscard]] static bool ImageRefusalEnds();
+
     /// ASTC decoded on the GPU and re-compressed to BC1/BC3 there (accelerate_astc=Gpu with
     /// astc_recompression=Bc1/Bc3): decode into a temporary RGBA8 image, encode, copy.
     void TranscodeAstcToBcn(Image& image, const StagingBufferRef& map,
